.TH MODBUS-SCRAPER 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-scraper \- Huawei SUN2000 Modbus TCP to Prometheus exporter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-scraper
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B modbus-scraper \-\-dry-run
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A stdlib-only Prometheus exporter that polls a Huawei SUN2000 inverter
over Modbus TCP and exposes the \fBhuawei_*\fR metrics the dashboard
expects, plus health gauges. It can poll the inverter directly or through
.BR modbus-cache (1)
(which it auto-detects and reports as the \fBhuawei_cache_*\fR
diagnostics). The exporter is the read-only consumer of the family: no
write path, no control surface; its HTTP surface is exactly two GET
routes (\fB/\fR and \fB/metrics\fR).
.PP
The exported metrics (names, HELP texts and profile bindings live in
\fBmetrics.json\fR): the PV generation, the grid export/import split, the
derived home consumption, the optional battery metrics (\fB--battery\fR),
\fBhuawei_up\fR, the error counter and the last-poll timestamp. Sanity
caps (\fB--max-kwp\fR, \fB--max-grid-kw\fR) turn impossible readings into
HTTP 503 until a good poll. Modbus TCP must be enabled on the
inverter/SDongle/EMMA (default port 502, unit id 1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
config file (ini, \fB[scraper]\fR section, snake_case keys). Default:
\fB$SCRAPER_CONFIG\fR, then \fBscraper.ini\fR next to the script, then the
packaged sample; a missing file is fine, a malformed one is fatal.
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics-spec " FILE"
the metrics spec JSON (name \(-> {help, type, profile?}). Default the
bundled \fBmetrics.json\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST" ", " \-\-modbus-port " N" ", " \-\-unit " N"
the upstream device. Defaults \fB127.0.0.1\fR, \fB5502\fR, \fB1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-modbus-offset " N"
added to register addresses (\fB\-1\fR for gateways that need 0-based
addressing). Default \fB0\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME|PATH"
the device profile (the register map); defaults to the bundled
\fBsun2000\fR. The explicit register flags below override the profile
when set.
.TP
.BI \-\-pv-register " ADDR" ", " \-\-grid-register " ADDR"
the PV input power (I32 W) and the grid/active power (I32 W) registers.
Defaults \fB32064\fR / \fB37113\fR (Huawei Issue 04; the 20200520 protocol
wants \fB32089\fR / \fB37258\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " X" ", " \-\-grid-scale " X"
raw-value multipliers (defaults \fB1\fR \(em the registers already report
watts; \fB1000\fR for kW devices).
.TP
.BI \-\-max-kwp " KW" ", " \-\-max-grid-kw " KW"
sanity caps (\fB6\fR / \fB12\fR); a reading past them (and any negative
PV) answers HTTP 503 until the data is sane again. \fB0\fR = off.
.TP
.B \-\-battery
enable battery support: the battery term in the home derivation and the
battery metrics.
.TP
.BI \-\-battery-register " ADDR" ", " \-\-battery-soc-register " ADDR"
battery power (I32 W, +charge) and SoC (U16, %\(en10). Defaults
\fB37001\fR / \fB37004\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-grid-positive-import
the grid register is positive on import (the default is export).
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " HOST:PORT"
exporter bind address. Default \fB127.0.0.1:9350\fR (loopback only).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " S"
seconds between Modbus polls. Default \fB5\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth-token " TOKEN" ", " \-\-auth-token-file " FILE"
require \fBAuthorization: Bearer\fR on every request (401 +
\fBWWW-Authenticate\fR otherwise); the file is re-read on every SIGHUP
(rotation = rewrite + reload). Mutually exclusive.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-clients " N" ", " \-\-client-timeout " S"
cap concurrent HTTP clients (default \fB64\fR; overflow answers 503) and
kick idle keep-alive connections (default \fB300\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-log-level " LEVEL" ", " \-\-local-time ", " \-\-log-access
logging: default \fBINFO\fR, UTC stamps, quiet HTTP (\fB--log-access\fR
logs every request at INFO). The scraper has no separate audit-trail
file \(em its log is the trail.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
validate the configuration and print the effective settings without
binding or contacting anything.
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
reload the configuration: interval, scales, caps, registers, the battery
flag, the auth token (the token file is re-read = rotation), the client
limits and the upstream address. The listen address, the log level and
\fBmetrics.json\fR need a restart.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
graceful shutdown with a session summary.
.SH LOGGING
UTC-stamped lines on stdout/stderr (journald omits its own stamp when the
service manager captures it). Reachability changes and reloads log at
INFO; rejected requests (unauthorized, rate-limited) always log with the
peer; the suite's rule is zero tracebacks.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SCRAPER_*
every flag has an environment twin (\fBSCRAPER_HOST\fR,
\fBSCRAPER_LISTEN\fR, \fBSCRAPER_AUTH_TOKEN\fR, ...); the flag wins over
the env, the env over the ini.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I scrape/scraper.ini ", " scrape/metrics.json
the packaged sample config and the metrics spec.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success (\fB--dry-run\fR: valid configuration).
.TP
.B 1
invalid configuration (reason on stderr).
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.
.SH EXAMPLES
Poll a cache proxy and scrape with a Prometheus job named \fBsun2000\fR:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-scraper --host 127.0.0.1 --modbus-port 15502
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-cache (1),
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1),
.BR dashboard (1)
.PP
\fBscrape/README.md\fR in the suite checkout \(em the metrics table, the
caps and the Prometheus setup.
